# Package lock files (regenerated during builds)
# package-lock.json is KEPT: this is an application, not a library. The
# lock is what makes an install reproducible — the same tree in the
# pipeline, in a worker's tree and on a person's machine — and it is what
# lets `npm ci` skip the resolver, which on npm 10.9 crashes outright
# resolving this frontend's peer graph from nothing.

